course: dictionary
lesson: 9546
title: Many meanings, one word
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, so you must read the words around them to find the right one. «He had to stoop to pick up the coin.» Here the clues are coin and pick up, so stoop means to bend your body forwards and down.
explain: The same word can name a habit. «The old man walked with a stoop.» Here a stoop is the way he holds his shoulders and head bent forward all the time. The word old and the word walked are your clues.
explain: Now look at «I would never stoop to cheating.» It does not mean bending at all. Stoop to means to do something bad or mean that is below your usual standards. Test it: "I would never bend down to cheating" does not make sense, so you know this is a different meaning.
explain: In the US and Canada, a stoop is a small set of steps in front of a house door, where people sit and talk. The sentence around the word tells you which meaning to choose.
fact: Stoop can be a verb or a noun.
fact: «Stoop» means to bend your body forwards and down.
fact: «Stoop to» means to do something bad or mean, below your usual standards, as in «stoops to lies».
fact: «A peregrine falcon dives in a stoop at over 300 km/h, the fastest speed of any animal.»
fact: In the US and Canada, a stoop is a small set of steps and a platform in front of a house door.
exercise: «He had to stoop to tie his shoelaces.» What does stoop mean here? | *To bend your body forwards and down | To climb up steep steps | To do something mean and below your standards | To jump high into the air
exercise: «An old man walked with a stoop.» What is a stoop here? | *A habit of holding your shoulders and head bent forward | A bad deed done to cheat someone | A small set of steps in front of a house door | A quick run down a hill
exercise: «I would never stoop to cheating.» What does stoop to mean here? | To sit down on the steps while cheating | *To do something mean that is below your usual standards | To jump over a fence
test: «The children sat on the front stoop after school.» Which meaning fits? | *A small set of steps and a platform in front of a house door | To do something below your standards | A habit of standing with your shoulders bent | To bend your body forwards and down
test: According to «A peregrine falcon dives in a stoop at over 300 km/h», how fast does the falcon dive? | About 30 km/h | *Over 300 km/h | About 3 km/h | Exactly 100 km/h
exam: Choose the meaning of stoop in «Tom would never stoop to lies.» | A small set of steps in front of a door | To stand up very straight | *To do something mean and below his usual standards | To bend down to tie a shoelace
